# Catch-all FIRST: every text file is LF in the repo and on checkout,
# regardless of core.autocrlf. Without it, a Windows checkout with
# autocrlf=true puts CRLF on disk and Prettier (endOfLine: "lf") fails
# every file, which short-circuits `prettier --check . && eslint .` so
# ESLint never runs - the fifth CRLF variant, see ONBOARDING.md.
# Order matters: in .gitattributes the LAST matching line wins, so the
# specific `binary`/`eol` rules below must come AFTER this line or the
# catch-all would override them (text=auto on a .pmtiles file).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Without this, Git falls back to content-sniffing heuristics to decide
# whether a file is text or binary - unreliable for a custom binary
# container format like PMTiles, and on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows' common default), a misdetected
# file gets its line-ending bytes silently rewritten, corrupting the
# archive. Explicit `binary` here overrides autocrlf for these paths
# regardless of any user/global git config. Found via a real Windows
# test: map polygons/lakes never rendered (map.json-driven DOM popups
# still worked, since those don't touch these files) - see ONBOARDING.md.
*.pmtiles binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
# mobile/android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar (Iteration 8+, Android
# POC) is the same class of risk - a binary format that must never go
# through autocrlf, added preemptively rather than waiting to hit it.
*.jar binary
# Same class of bug again, a third variant: shell scripts checked out
# with CRLF (Git for Windows' common autocrlf=true default) break when
# actually run, even though they're plain text - found running
# data/scripts/fetch-natural-earth.sh from WSL against this same Windows
# checkout: `set -euo pipefail` failed with "pipefail: invalid option
# name" because the trailing \r attached itself to the option name.
# `text eol=lf` forces LF on checkout regardless of platform/autocrlf,
# for every shell script including gradlew (POSIX shell despite no .sh
# extension) which has hit the identical CRLF corruption already, just
# not yet exercised by a Linux/WSL-side gradle invocation.
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
# Windows batch files (mobile/android/gradlew.bat) stay CRLF - cmd.exe
# has known label/goto parsing bugs on LF-only batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
